    "body": "With a 720p source, all my cutpoints from MythTV are exact, but the audio still gets delayed.\r\n\r\nSource:\r\n<pre>  Duration: 01:02:59.97, start: 73839.401322, bitrate: 4492 kb/s\r\n  Program 1 \r\n  Stream #0:0[0x425]: Video: h264 (High) ([27][0][0][0] / 0x001B), yuv420p(tv, bt709, progressive), 1280x720 [SAR 1:1 DAR 16:9], Closed Captions, 59.94 fps, 59.94 tbr, 90k tbn, 119.88 tbc\r\n  Stream #0:1[0x426](eng): Audio: ac3 (AC-3 / 0x332D4341), 48000 Hz, 5.1(side), fltp, 384 kb/s\r\n  Stream #0:2[0x427](spa): Audio: ac3 (AC-3 / 0x332D4341), 48000 Hz, stereo, fltp, 192 kb/s</pre>\r\n\r\nResult:\r\n<pre>  Stream #0:0(und): Video: h264 (High) (avc1 / 0x31637661), yuv420p(tv, bt709), 1280x720 [SAR 1:1 DAR 16:9], Closed Captions, 4105 kb/s, 59.96 fps, 59.94 tbr, 90k tbn, 239.76 tbc (default)\r\n  Stream #0:1(eng): Audio: ac3 (ac-3 / 0x332D6361), 48000 Hz, 5.1(side), fltp, 384 kb/s (default)\r\n  Stream #0:2(spa): Audio: ac3 (ac-3 / 0x332D6361), 48000 Hz, stereo, fltp, 192 kb/s</pre>\r\n\r\nThe result references 59.96fps instead of 59.94fps.  If the video is playing back 0.02 fps to fast, that might explain the audio sync.",
